#version 450

// Contract resource for lucerna.denoise.diffuse real shader-output evidence.
// See shader_generated_diffuse_output_contract.glsl for the concrete future
// output-image interface and readiness gates.
//
// This file is intentionally side-effect free until the render scheduler binds a
// real denoise output path. It documents the shader-side inputs and outputs
// controller validation should assert before flipping realDenoiseShaderOutput to
// true in Java/runtime telemetry.
//
// Expected readable inputs:
// - lucerna.lighting.direct
// - lucerna.lighting.diffuseGi
// - lucerna.lighting.cacheConfidence
// - lucerna.lighting.variance
// - lucerna.lighting.rayBudget
// - lucerna.gbuffer.depth
// - lucerna.gbuffer.normalRoughness
// - lucerna.gbuffer.materialId
// - lucerna.gbuffer.motionHistory
// - PreviousDepth
// - PreviousNormalRoughness
// - PreviousLighting
// - MotionHistory
// - VarianceConfidence
//
// Expected writable outputs once implemented:
// - lucerna.denoise.diffuse, full-resolution linear diffuse radiance
// - lucerna.denoise.rejectionMask, full-resolution temporal/edge rejection mask
// - lucerna.denoise.historyRejectionMask, optional debug mask explaining why
//   history was rejected at depth/normal/material/motion boundaries
// - lucerna.denoise.rawVsDenoisedQuality, optional debug target used only for
//   controller proof that raw GI and shader-denoised GI differ for the right
//   reasons
//
// Shader-side edge-aware output contract:
// - Raw input is lucerna.lighting.diffuseGi plus direct/cache/variance metadata;
//   CPU/readback preview payloads are not valid producers for this pass.
// - Current-frame material identity is a required geometry rejection input:
//   lucerna.gbuffer.materialId must be bound alongside depth, normal/roughness,
//   motion/history, confidence, and variance before output readiness is true.
// - Geometry edges must be rejected with current and previous depth, normals,
//   material id, motion vectors, variance/confidence, and history validity.
// - The full-resolution diffuse output must be generated by shader execution
//   into lucerna.denoise.diffuse, not by drawing a preview texture into the
//   borrowed Minecraft/Sodium color target.
// - lucerna.denoise.rejectionMask must explain temporal, material, disocclusion,
//   confidence, and variance rejection separately enough for debug overlay use.
//
// Candidate-output boundary:
// - shaderDenoiseOutputImageCandidateReady may only mean a CPU-staged or
//   non-GPU candidate image exists for inspection.
// - shaderDenoiseOutputImageReady and realShaderDenoiseOutputReady require this
//   pass to own a writable shader output image/material and to write it from
//   shader execution. The current runtime-loadable route is a public Mojang
//   fragment pass into an owned color target; a later compute route may use
//   storage-image dispatch with the barriers described in layout.json.
// - The real-output prerequisite bundle must stay explicit in telemetry:
//   shaderDenoiseInputPrerequisitesReady,
//   shaderDenoiseOutputImageReadinessReady,
//   shaderDenoiseTemporalHistoryReady, and
//   shaderDenoiseRealOutputPrerequisitesReady.
// - Readiness must name each real-output handoff explicitly:
//   shaderDenoiseOutputImageOwnedByShaderPass=true,
//   shaderDenoiseColorAttachmentWrite=true for the current public Mojang
//   fragment route, shaderDenoiseOutputBarrierReady=true, and
//   shaderDenoiseOutputFinalCompositeConsumable=true. These fields stay false
//   for CPU/readback output, public Mojang visual draws, and candidate-only
//   images even when those paths produce visible pixels.
// - shaderDenoiseOutputStorageWritable=true is reserved for a future compute or
//   storage-image route; the current fragment color-attachment output must keep
//   shaderDenoiseComputeDispatch=false and shaderDenoiseStorageImageWrite=false.
// - Candidate-only images must keep shaderDenoiseShaderGeneratedOutput=false and
//   must not be consumed by final composite as a real shader-generated target.
// - CPU/readback guided visual denoise should be reported as a fallback/source
//   identity, not as lucerna.denoise.diffuse readiness.
//
// Evidence boundary:
// - realDenoiseShaderOutput=false while this resource remains contract-only.
// - CPU/readback denoised GI payloads must be reported separately.
// - A future implementation or the current public Mojang fragment route must
//   write the outputs from shader execution, then
//   controller validation can compare raw-GI, shader-denoised, final, and debug
//   screenshots/logs without relying on preview draw substitution.
// - Quality proof must include edge-preservation, history rejection,
//   variance/confidence, and raw-vs-denoised comparisons. A full-screen blur or
//   rectangular preview wash is explicitly insufficient.
// - No-overclaim markers required while this file is side-effect free:
//   shaderDenoiseOutputImageCandidateBoundaryOnly=true,
//   realShaderDenoiseOutputProven=false, and
//   shaderDenoiseOverclaimPresent=false.
//
// Placeholder policy: this contract file has no storage writes, image writes,
// atomics, barriers, discard, color output, or depth output. The paired
// denoise/shader_generated_diffuse_output.fsh resource owns the first public
// Mojang color-output form and is not compute denoise.
void main() {
}
